{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he shall not come for any dead soul.</b> A warning to the high priest not to enter the tent of the dead. Now I know only the high priest, who is warned by לא יבא; from where do I include the ordinary priest? Through a gezeirah shavah: לא יטמא mentioned in the case of the ordinary priest (כ״ה) from לא יטמא mentioned in the case of the high priest (כ״ג): just as לא יטמא said of the high priest is also warned by לא יבא, so too לא יטמא said of the ordinary priest is also warned by לא יבא. Thus far." "<b>For his father and for his mother he shall not defile himself.</b> The verse comes only to permit him a met mitzvah. Here it goes without saying, for his son and his daughter, for his brother and his sister — if he does not defile himself for his father and his mother, כ״ש that he does not defile himself for other relatives."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The abbreviations כ״ה and כ״ג are resolved as כהן הדיוט (ordinary priest) and כהן גדול (high priest) respectively; ג״‎ש as גזירה שוה (gezeirah shavah); ת״‎כ as תן כן (a standard tannaitic conclusion formula)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:08.673061955Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}